WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.147 --> 00:00:05.730
PETER MANUELIAN: So how did the Gods appear?

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:09.600
How did they provide these
predictions and these oracles?

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.610
Well for the average
Egyptian, they would

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.330
have to wait until the statue of the
God was brought out of the temple.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.460
So inside the sanctuary at
Karnak and many other places,

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.800
there was a statue of the God that had
to be ritually clothed and ritually fed

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.330
every day by the priests.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.700
And then, on certain
festival days, the statue

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.520
was placed inside a
bark or a sacred boat

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.480
and hoisted up on the shoulders of the
priests and marched out of the temple.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.440
And it's at that point when this statue
was brought across the river visiting

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.450
other shrines and other
temples, there would

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.940
be parades on either side of the Nile.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.900
This was the beautiful Festival of
the Valley, or the Festival of Opet,

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.320
and this is when individuals
might approach with a petition.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.960
Yea or nay, am I in
good shape, has someone

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.600
stolen from me, what about
this cow that I bought, have I

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.330
paid on the installment plan
correctly, or is someone

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.750
throwing an accusation at me, what
should I do, all kinds of questions

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:01.890
would come.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.280
So how would the god indicate
what the right thing to do was?

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.824
The hieroglyphs talked about
nodding in approval or disapproval

00:01:08.824 --> 00:01:11.490
and there's some disagreement
about whether the statues actually

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:15.340
had some moving parts and might
invoke their head a little bit.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.280
That is probably unlikely.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.420
More likely is that the statue in its
bark would be brought by the priest

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:25.170
either forward to say yes,
or backwards to say no,

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.130
or perhaps leaned to one side or another
if there are two competing petitions

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:33.421
brought, and this is how the God
would signal approval or disapproval.

00:01:33.421 --> 00:01:35.670
And of course, I can't help
wondering about corruption

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.753
because all you need to do is bribe
these priests who are holding the bark

00:01:38.753 --> 00:01:41.550
and holding the statue to
lean to one side or the other

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:44.910
to favor one case against
another case of course.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:49.630
So oracles and predictions, the
individuals, the populace in Luxor,

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:53.490
or ancient Thebes, would be approaching
the god with very, very high hopes

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.530
to get the results that they desire.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:59.160
The kings would be petitioning in
a much more private way, of course,

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:03.840
and these outcomes would be recorded for
all time in their temple inscriptions

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:08.669
to show that yes, they are the divinely
born next rulers on the throne,

00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:11.009
they are on the throne
with all legitimacy,

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:13.080
or the decisions they've
made for this expedition

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.790
or that campaign were
absolutely justified.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:19.020
So it's a good backup system
to bolster your kingship.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.370
[MUSIC PLAYING]

